<title>SPAIN: Spain's Sol Melia 1996 net profit up 56 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Sol Melia 1996 net profit up 56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for Spanish hotel chain Sol Melia for 1996 (in billion of pesetas):</p>
<p>					    DEC 1996   DEC 1995  PCT CHG</p>
<p>    Revenues				11.48	9.82     16.9</p>
<p>    Operating expenses		   5.38	4.74     13.5</p>
<p>    Profit from ordinary activities  6.15	4.46     37.8</p>
<p>    Profit before taxes, minorities  6.13	4.49     36.6</p>
<p>    Group net profit		     4.80	3.08     56.0</p>
<p>    Parent company profit		4.75	2.97     60.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name Sol Melia Hoteles SA. Shares in Spain's leading hotel group started trading on Madrid's stock exchange in July 1996. The group said in a statement it was moderately optimistic about its European Resort Division for 1997 given the outlook for the pound and negotiations with Sol Melia's main tour operators.</p>
<p>The company said its corporate tax rate for 1996 was substantially lower than forecast due to the increasing proportion of foreign income, the special tax regime applicable to earnings from the hotels in the Canary islands and the deduction of certain expenses.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
